{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"Herring, the Miser: a past life story","html":"<article id='ja78'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Jātaka </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Stories of Past Lives 78 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Ekakanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Ones </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Varuṇavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Warding Tree </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>8. Illisajātaka </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Herring, the Miser: a past life story </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Ubho khañjā ubho kuṇī, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Both are lame, both crippled, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>ubho visamacakkhukā; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>both cross-eyed, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Ubhinnaṁ piḷakā jātā, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>and both covered in warts: </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>nāhaṁ passāmi illisan”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>I see not which is Herring. </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>Illisajātakaṁ aṭṭhamaṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
